------ Deferred from the /pitching + /batting restructure ------
SECURITY: /storage/schools/<slug>/... routes are unauthenticated
  app/main.py:96-106 -- the three send_from_directory routes have no
  @login_required and never check the slug against current_user.school.slug.
  Anyone who guesses a path downloads another school's charts. PDFs are already
  safe (exports stream via send_file behind the login); chart PNGs are not.
  Fix: require login + verify the slug matches, or serve charts through an
  authenticated route the way /api/*/export does.

outings.date is String(20) holding dates -- should be db.Date
  Works today only because ISO strings sort chronologically. Needs a migration
  plus a look at the dashboard queries in app/routes/pages.py. Blocks proper
  date arithmetic (e.g. "last 30 days") on the DB side.

PDF header subtitle format is wrong for multi-game reports
  generate_header hardcodes "{a} @ {b}" (report_lab_generator.py:145), giving
  "HOME @ 2 games" on hitter reports and "HOME @ AWAY" on pitching ones -- the
  latter is also backwards from the away-@-home convention, inherited from the
  old upload.py call. Make the separator a parameter so each report type picks
  its own ("vs" for aggregated ranges, "@" for a true single away game).

Rule learned: any change to game_archive._build_entry needs a
  `flask --app app.main rebuild-game-index` run, or existing archives silently
  report defaults for the new field instead of real values.

